y = \\ln (2x+1).\n$$\n\nFirst notice that this function can be written as the composite function\n\n$$\ny = \\ln u, \\qquad u = 2x+1.\n$$\n\nWe can use the chain rule to compute the derivative of this composite function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡u)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{u}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $u=2x+1,$ we obtain the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2}{2x+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093370 #edb/ref 1065 1272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093370 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "054d5bfc-280f-5da5-9576-4b4cd8668e78" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093370 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233100 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107469" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233100 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233100 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}(4-2x)$ at the point $(1,\\operatorname{ln}2).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233100 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e624a42e-febd-5a83-813e-03b578dd4b5f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233100 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=\\operatorname{ln}u,\\,u=4-2x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-2.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-2x}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{4-2x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\cancel{2}}{\\cancel{2}\\cdot (2-x)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line at the point where $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={-\\frac{1}{2-x}|}_{x=1}=-\\frac{1}{2-1}=-1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the slope of the tangent line at the point $(1,\\operatorname{ln}2)$ is $m=-1.$ Now, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-\\operatorname{ln}2 & =-1(x-1) \\\\ y & =-x+1+\\operatorname{ln}2\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186428027 #edb/ref 1030 0.5 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186428027 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 2 eligible passed source activities = 0.500000; nearest selected fraction = 1/2. Crossing activity numbers [2]; waits [2]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1/2 (1/2). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: True. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/foundations-frequency-estimates.json, pair 1036->332. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relationships.json." #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186428027 #edb/ref 1036 #edb/ref 17592186050711 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186490400 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186490410 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186490400 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186490400 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $f(x)=12\\ln(2 x)$ at the point $(12,12 \\log{\\left(24 \\right)}).$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186490400 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "23758b8b-9bec-5ac3-b6e8-fa4ac19c5bfc" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186490400 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$ f=12\\ln u,\\,u=2 x.$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{12}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2.$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} &=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ &=\\frac{12}{u}\\cdot(2) \\\\ &=\\frac{12}{2 x}\\cdot(2) \\\\ &=\\frac{12}{x}.\\end{aligned}$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line at the point where $x=12$ is\n\n$$m=\\left.(\\frac{12}{x})\\right|_{x=12}=1.$$\n\nHence, the slope of the tangent line at the point $(12,12 \\log{\\left(24 \\right)})$ is $m=1.$ Now, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}y-y_1 &=m(x-x_1) \\\\ y-(12 \\log{\\left(24 \\right)}) &=(1)(x-(12)) \\\\ y &=x - 12 + 12 \\log{\\left(24 \\right)}.\\end{aligned}$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186490408 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186490399 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186490408 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186490408 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $f(x)=\\ln(21 - x)$ at the point $(20,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186490408 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9e9f5055-f5c3-5e44-823d-b027109ff59f" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186490408 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$ f=\\ln u,\\,u=21 - x.$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-1.$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} &=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot(-1) \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{21 - x}\\cdot(-1) \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{x - 21}.\\end{aligned}$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line at the point where $x=20$ is\n\n$$m=\\left.(\\frac{1}{x - 21})\\right|_{x=20}=-1.$$\n\nHence, the slope of the tangent line at the point $(20,0)$ is $m=-1.$ Now, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}y-y_1 &=m(x-x_1) \\\\ y-(0) &=(-1)(x-(20)) \\\\ y &=20 - x.\\end{aligned}$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186490412 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186092264.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186490412 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "8de5755c-8fed-5bec-b71d-9b4da06c0dd4" #edb/ref 17592186045443]}
